# This directory is intentionally empty for now.
#
# It must exist: `Package.swift` declares a `JanelaWorkspaceTests` target, and
# SwiftPM fails to resolve if the directory is missing. Git does not track empty
# directories, so this file is what keeps it alive across a clone. Delete it once
# there is a real test file here.
#
# What belongs here (see docs/testing.md):
#
#   - All four `WorkspaceCreationRequest` cases, using an in-memory database and a
#     FAKE `WorktreeServing` — these tests are about orchestration, not git.
#   - The product rule that worktree creation is one case of `createWorkspace`,
#     not a separate path. If someone adds a second public creation method, that
#     should be visible here.
#   - `removalPlan`: that it reports live sessions, that `canDeleteDirectory` is
#     true ONLY for `.managedWorktree`, and that an adopted worktree is never
#     offered for deletion.
#   - `removeWorkspace`: that it never deletes a directory unless the plan
#     explicitly opted in.
#   - `ShellEnvironment`: that login-shell argv[0] is prefixed with `-` (this is
#     what makes the user's PATH work), and that the JANELA_* variables are set.
